<title>INDIA: India Karur Vysya 96/97 net rises - PTI.</title>
<headline>India Karur Vysya 96/97 net rises - PTI.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Karur Vysya Bank has reported a net profit of 360.6 million rupees for 1996/97 (April-March), compared with 322.4 million in the previous year, the Press Trust of India (PTI) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bank's board of directors recommended an enhanced dividend of 50 percent per share, the news agency said. It did not give the dividend rate for 1995/96.</p>
<p>The bank's deposits grew to 15.75 billion rupees from 11.59 billion, while advances grew to 9.56 billion rupees from 8.24 billion, PTI said. ($1=35.8 rupees)</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom, +91-11-301 2024</p>
